Make the state datamodem keeps outside its per-call structures thread-local.

datamodem runs one call at a time, so the vendored V.42 keeps some link
state in plain globals: why a link went down, how many damaged frames
arrived, which ADP the far end sent, the detection state (dm_neg, whose
idle_run steers detection itself), and the side table of what spandsp's
v42_state_t has no room for (dm_xid). Asterisk runs a modem per channel,
concurrently, each on its own channel thread, and every access to these is
from the thread pumping that channel's audio - so thread-local storage gives
each call its own copy with no other change in behaviour. The test hooks
beside them stay global: they are set from the environment, the same for
every call.

